---
/*
 * Use cases · the shape of the problem.
 *
 * Four tabs: Recruiting, Finance & Compliance, Logistics, Insurance Ops.
 * Same product-screenshot card layout as v1. Tabs swap via a small inline
 * script at the bottom of the file — same .on-class pattern as v1.
 */
---

<section class="uc-sec" id="use-cases">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="s-head">
      <div class="left">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span>The shape of problem we solve</span>
        <h2>Not four industries.<br />One <em>problem shape</em>.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="right">
        <p>Each engagement below is a different vertical — but they're the same problem: long-tail operational work that's too custom for SaaS, too operational for a consultancy, and too plumbing-heavy for AI coding tools. That's the surface the delivery door covers.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="shape-frame">
      <b>The pattern, in plain words</b>
      Per-record judgment work. Driven by rules and conversation. Audited end-to-end. Routed to a named human when the call isn't black and white. Generates a report at the end. That shape shows up across recruiting, banking, logistics, and insurance — under different names.
    </div>

    <div class="uc-tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="on" data-uc="recruiting" type="button">Recruiting</button>
      <button data-uc="finance" type="button">Finance & Compliance</button>
      <button data-uc="logistics" type="button">Logistics</button>
      <button data-uc="ops" type="button">Insurance Ops</button>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Recruiting ────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="uc-panel on" data-panel="recruiting">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">High-volume staffing</span>
        <h3>Conversational follow-up at the scale of every placement.</h3>
        <p class="lede">
          Mid-market staffing firms place thousands of contractors a year. The work after placement — check-ins, engagement calls, redeployment — is conversational and per-person. Recruiters never get to it. Assembly does.
        </p>
        <div class="uc-stats">
          <div>
            <div class="k">Contractors</div>
            <div class="v">10,000<small>placed per year</small></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="k">Redeployment lift</div>
            <div class="v">+5%<small>vs. baseline</small></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="k">Annual gross profit</div>
            <div class="v">$2.0M<small>at $4K margin / redeploy</small></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="uc-list">
          <li>Week-1 check-in calls — conversational, contextual to assignment</li>
          <li>Monthly engagement & satisfaction conversations</li>
          <li>End-of-assignment redeployment outreach</li>
          <li>Time-card nudges and dispute resolution flow</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="uc-art lift">
          <img src="/dashboard-agents.png" alt="Assembly Studio — capabilities" />
          <div class="cap">
            <b>Studio · Agents</b>
            <span>Live customer environment</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Finance & Compliance ──────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="uc-panel" data-panel="finance">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Regulated banking</span>
        <h3>Continuous compliance testing with auditor-grade lineage.</h3>
        <p class="lede">
          Regional banks run programs for Reg E, supervisory trade controls, AML. Assembly automates the deterministic portions and routes judgment to named reviewers — every finding traceable to its source record.
        </p>
        <div class="uc-stats">
          <div>
            <div class="k">Controls tested</div>
            <div class="v">11<small>per quarterly run</small></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="k">Sample population</div>
            <div class="v">5,855<small>claims, quarterly</small></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="k">Audit lineage</div>
            <div class="v">100%<small>findings traceable</small></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="uc-list">
          <li>Sampling, threshold math, business-day arithmetic</li>
          <li>Federal Reserve calendar & CFPB rule pack evaluation</li>
          <li>HITL disposition routed to named compliance reviewer</li>
          <li>CMP report generation in customer's audit format</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="uc-art lift">
          <img src="/dashboard-console.png" alt="Assembly Console — Reg E run" />
          <div class="cap">
            <b>Console · Reg E Run</b>
            <span>Axos Bank · live</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Logistics ─────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="uc-panel" data-panel="logistics">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Mid-market logistics</span>
        <h3>Carrier exceptions, resolved before they become claims.</h3>
        <p class="lede">
          Most shipments are quiet. The 8% that aren't — missed pickups, dimensional re-rates, accessorial disputes — are where margin leaks. Assembly reads the EDI, talks to the carrier, drafts the dispute, and routes judgment calls to your team.
        </p>
        <div class="uc-stats">
          <div>
            <div class="k">Exceptions / month</div>
            <div class="v">~14k<small>typical mid-market book</small></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="k">Auto-resolved</div>
            <div class="v">72%<small>conversational + rules</small></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="k">Avg recovery</div>
            <div class="v">$118<small>per disputed shipment</small></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="uc-list">
          <li>EDI 214 / 990 ingestion · exception classification</li>
          <li>Carrier portal browser automation for dispute filing</li>
          <li>Re-rate and accessorial review with HITL above threshold</li>
          <li>Weekly recovery report & carrier scorecard</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="uc-art lift">
          <div class="exq">
            <div class="exq-h">
              <span class="eyebrow">Exception queue · today</span>
              <span class="eyebrow accent">14 routed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="exq-rows">
              <div class="exq-row alt">
                <b>SHP-49102</b>
                <span>Accessorial · liftgate · re-rate pending</span>
                <span class="badge auto">AUTO</span>
              </div>
              <div class="exq-row">
                <b>SHP-49114</b>
                <span>Missed pickup · driver no-show 2026-04-29</span>
                <span class="badge hitl">HITL</span>
              </div>
              <div class="exq-row alt">
                <b>SHP-49118</b>
                <span>Dim re-rate · 48×40×52 contested</span>
                <span class="badge auto">AUTO</span>
              </div>
              <div class="exq-row">
                <b>SHP-49121</b>
                <span>Damage claim · photo evidence required</span>
                <span class="badge hitl">HITL</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="cap">
            <b>Console · Exception queue</b>
            <span>Mid-market logistics</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ── Insurance Ops ─────────────────────────────────────────── -->
    <div class="uc-panel" data-panel="ops">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Insurance operations</span>
        <h3>First-notice-of-loss to file open, without the queue.</h3>
        <p class="lede">
          FNOL is a conversation: listen, classify, collect what's missing, open the file. Assembly handles it on voice and text, populates the system of record, and only escalates the calls that need a human adjuster.
        </p>
        <div class="uc-stats">
          <div>
            <div class="k">FNOLs / day</div>
            <div class="v">~3,200<small>regional carrier</small></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="k">Time-to-file</div>
            <div class="v">&minus;68%<small>median, vs. call center</small></div>
          </div>
          <div>
            <div class="k">CSAT</div>
            <div class="v">4.7/5<small>post-conversation</small></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <ul class="uc-list">
          <li>Voice + text intake with state-by-state required-field rules</li>
          <li>Coverage check & classification against policy data</li>
          <li>Open file in Guidewire / Duck Creek with full transcript</li>
          <li>Escalation to adjuster only when judgment is required</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="uc-art lift">
          <div class="fnol">
            <div class="fnol-h">
              <span class="eyebrow">FNOL · live transcript</span>
              <span class="eyebrow sage">&#9679; connected</span>
            </div>
            <div class="fnol-body">
              <div class="fnol-turn">
                <span class="t-who">CALLER</span>
                <span class="t-text">Hi, I need to report a fender bender from yesterday afternoon&hellip;</span>
              </div>
              <div class="fnol-turn">
                <span class="t-who t-bot">ASSEMBLY</span>
                <span class="t-text t-bot-text">Sorry to hear that. I'll get you opened up. Do you have your policy number, or want me to look you up by name and ZIP?</span>
              </div>
              <div class="fnol-turn">
                <span class="t-who">CALLER</span>
                <span class="t-text">Name and ZIP. It's Maria Davenport, 92708.</span>
              </div>
              <div class="fnol-match">
                <div class="m-row"><span>POLICY MATCH</span><b>CA-OTOA-44192</b></div>
                <div class="m-row"><span>COVERAGE</span><b class="ok">collision · in-force</b></div>
                <div class="m-row"><span>FILE</span><b class="ind">CL-2026-008341 · opened</b></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="cap">
            <b>Conversational · FNOL</b>
            <span>Regional auto carrier</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const tabs = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".uc-tabs button");
  const panels = document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".uc-panel");
  tabs.forEach((b) =>
    b.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const k = b.dataset.uc;
      tabs.forEach((x) => x.classList.toggle("on", x === b));
      panels.forEach((p) => p.classList.toggle("on", p.dataset.panel === k));
    }),
  );
</script>

<style>
  .uc-sec {
    padding: 120px 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ink-100);
  }

  .s-head {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
    gap: 80px;
    margin-bottom: 64px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (max-width: 920px) {
    .s-head { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 24px; }
  }
  .s-head .left .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 14px; display: block; }
  .s-head .left h2 { margin-top: 18px; }
  .s-head .left h2 em {
    font-style: normal;
    color: var(--color-indigo-600);
  }
  .s-head .right p {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    font-size: 18px;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .shape-frame {
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-ink-300);
    background: var(--color-ink-50);
    font-size: 14.5px;
    color: var(--color-ink-700);
    max-width: 780px;
  }
  .shape-frame b {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--color-ink-950);
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    font-size: 14px;
  }

  .uc-tabs {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }
  .uc-tabs button {
    padding: 10px 16px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-ink-700);
    background: #fff;
    transition: all 0.15s;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: inherit;
  }
  .uc-tabs button:hover {
    border-color: var(--color-ink-400);
  }
  .uc-tabs button.on {
    background: var(--color-ink-950);
    color: #fff;
    border-color: var(--color-ink-950);
  }

  .uc-panel {
    display: none;
    grid-template-columns: 1.05fr 0.95fr;
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .uc-panel.on { display: grid; }
  @media (max-width: 1000px) {
    .uc-panel.on { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 36px; }
  }

  .uc-panel h3 {
    font-size: 36px;
    letter-spacing: -0.022em;
    margin-top: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }
  .uc-panel .lede {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    font-size: 17px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .uc-stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
  }
  .uc-stats > div {
    padding: 20px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200);
  }
  .uc-stats > div:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .uc-stats .k {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .uc-stats .v {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: 30px;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.1;
    color: var(--color-ink-950);
  }
  .uc-stats .v small {
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    letter-spacing: 0;
    margin-top: 6px;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .uc-list {
    margin-top: 24px;
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    gap: 10px;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .uc-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    gap: 14px;
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--color-ink-700);
  }
  .uc-list li::before {
    content: "";
    display: block;
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--color-indigo-100);
    border: 3px solid var(--color-indigo-600);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  /* ── Product artifact card (used for image + custom mocks) ──── */
  .uc-art {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-card);
  }
  .uc-art img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }
  .uc-art .cap {
    padding: 14px 18px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-ink-100);
    background: var(--color-ink-50);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }
  .uc-art .cap b {
    color: var(--color-ink-950);
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    text-transform: none;
  }

  /* ── Exception queue mock (logistics) ──────────────────────── */
  .exq {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 28px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .exq-h {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .exq-h .accent { color: var(--color-indigo-600); }
  .exq-rows {
    display: grid;
    gap: 8px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }
  .exq-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 90px 1fr auto;
    gap: 14px;
    padding: 12px;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-ink-200);
    border-radius: 8px;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .exq-row.alt { background: var(--color-ink-50); }
  .exq-row b {
    color: var(--color-ink-950);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .exq-row span:not(.badge) {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
  }
  .badge {
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  }
  .badge.auto {
    color: var(--color-sage-fg);
    background: var(--color-sage-bg);
  }
  .badge.hitl {
    color: var(--color-amber-fg);
    background: var(--color-amber-bg);
  }

  /* ── FNOL transcript mock (insurance ops) ──────────────────── */
  .fnol {
    background: #fff;
    padding: 28px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 16px;
  }
  .fnol-h {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
  }
  .fnol-h .sage { color: var(--color-sage-fg); }
  .fnol-body {
    font-family: var(--font-body);
    font-size: 14px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .fnol-turn {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 70px 1fr;
    gap: 12px;
  }
  .t-who {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .t-who.t-bot { color: var(--color-indigo-600); }
  .t-text {
    color: var(--color-ink-700);
  }
  .t-text.t-bot-text { color: var(--color-ink-950); }
  .fnol-match {
    margin-top: 6px;
    padding: 14px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--color-ink-200);
    border-radius: 8px;
    display: grid;
    gap: 6px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
  }
  .m-row {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }
  .m-row span {
    color: var(--color-ink-500);
  }
  .m-row b {
    color: var(--color-ink-950);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .m-row b.ok { color: var(--color-sage-fg); }
  .m-row b.ind { color: var(--color-indigo-600); }

  .lift {
    transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease;
  }
  .lift:hover {
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-hover);
  }
</style>
